Kernel UAPI (clean-room)
------------------------

Original pure-Zig traffic-control (netem qdisc) rtnetlink client, clean-room
from the documented kernel UAPI headers `linux/rtnetlink.h` (`struct tcmsg`,
`TCA_*`) and `linux/pkt_sched.h` (`struct tc_netem_qopt` and friends,
`TCA_NETEM_*`), both **GPL-2.0 WITH Linux-syscall-note**.

No GPL header source is copied — only the uncopyrightable ABI facts they
document are used (struct layouts, command/attribute/flag constants). The
operative mechanism is the same Linux-syscall-note exception already relied on
by `netlink`/`wireguard`: it explicitly permits userspace of ANY license to use
these headers to interface with the kernel, which is why this module is cleanly
MIT despite citing GPL-2.0 headers.

Design reference — iproute2
---------------------------

The v1 (netem-only) client needed no third-party design reference; the v2
classful/filter work does.

iproute2 (**GPL-2.0-or-later**) — `tc/tc_core.c` (`tc_calc_xmittime`,
`tc_calc_rtable`, `tc_core_init`), `tc/q_htb.c`, `tc/q_tbf.c`,
`tc/q_fq_codel.c`, `tc/f_u32.c`, `tc/tc_class.c`, `tc/tc_filter.c` and
`lib/utils.c` (`__get_hz`) were consulted as a BEHAVIOUR reference for the
psched rate-table arithmetic, the default burst/buffer formulas, attribute
emission order and the client-side dump-filter rules.

No source was copied: the algorithms are re-derived and re-expressed (the rate
tables are evaluated exactly in u128 rather than iproute2's platform-dependent
double), and the byte-exact goldens captured from a real `tc` binary are the
independent check that the behaviour matches.
